messages:
sam: Thinking about a 'proto-slope' canary pattern — gateway keeps a small slope config (start_pct, step_pct, step_ms) and advances automatically based on telemetry (p95, 5xx rate, cost-per-token). Question: should the gateway own the slope advancement or should the control plane be the single source-of-truth?
maia: Prefer control-plane for rollout orchestration. keep gateway thin (evaluate, report), CP makes long-lived decisions.
derek: but we need sub-second local reaction when an upstream hotspot appears. gateway should be able to pause/rollback immediately without waiting on CP.
jin: agree on a declarative proto so both sides share the contract. proto-slope sounds like a nice SLA-oriented config. sketch below:
```proto
message SlopePolicy {
  string name = 1;
  uint32 start_pct = 2; // e.g. 5
  uint32 step_pct = 3;  // e.g. 5
  uint32 step_ms = 4;   // time between steps
  MetricTarget p95_target = 5;
  MetricThreshold error_rate_threshold = 6;
  bool gateway_allowed = 7; // can gateway autonomously advance?
}
message MetricTarget {
  string metric = 1; // "p95_latency_ms"
  uint32 target = 2;
}
message MetricThreshold {
  string metric = 1; // "5xx_rate"
  double threshold = 2;
}
```
alex: Console/UX needs: live slope progress bar, SLO vs slope chart, one-click rollback, and per-tenant override. also surface estimated cost delta per step.
sam: Proto snippet -> nice. telemetry naming: emit canary.metric.{slope_name}.{variant} with tags {instance, tenant, pct}. fields: p95, p50, error_rate, cost_per_token. then console can aggregate easily.
maia: Concern: if gateway has full rollout logic we increase test surface and risk. keep the gateway logic minimal: state machine {advancing, paused, rollback}. CP still records decisions and is authoritative. gateway can act on local severe faults immediately.
derek: implementation detail: gateway state machine must be idempotent and able to recover after restart. leader election for advance decisions sounds heavy — alternative: gateways propose -> CP authorizes advance token.
jin: good point. maybe gateways only propose candidate advances (based on local telemetry). CP validates aggregated metrics and issues a signed "advance" token the gateway consumes. avoids split-brain.
deploy-bot: deploy-bot: canary started proto-slope/v0.1 -> 5% :rocket:
alex: Action items: jin -> spike proto defs and token flow (owner), maia -> test plan for gateway safety and chaos tests, sam -> telemetry event schema + dashboard panel, derek -> leader/approval implementation options. I'll mock UX & place in Figma.
sam: :thumbsup: quick-win: publish proto and a console widget to visualize slope live so we can iterate on heuristics.
